[5] Proof readout
  1. Arc topology fails on exactly two residual same-topology buckets,
     and the failing rows are four single-swap collars at drops 9 and 11.
  2. In each collar, the covering row has zero primitive safe mass for
     q<=13, while the q-witness row has first primitive safe q equal
     to its dropped speed and its q-witness threshold.
  3. The coarse largest-safe-component stalk splits both topology
     exceptions, so the exceptions are owner-strip repairs rather than
     new boundary/open or route-label debt.
  4. Candidate lemma: if a post-status residual coarse ET+unit fiber is
     not split by compact arc topology, then it is an owner-stalk collar
     whose primitive q<=13 deck also splits the Q-witness/covering route.
